VVEERRSSIIOONNSS
       AppleTalk  is  supported  by Linux 2.0 or higher.  The _/_p_r_o_c interfaces
       exist since Linux 2.2.

NNOOTTEESS
       Be very careful with the SSOO__BBRROOAADDCCAASSTT option; it is not  privileged  in
       Linux.   It  is  easy  to overload the network with careless sending to
       broadcast addresses.

   CCoommppaattiibbiilliittyy
       The basic AppleTalk socket interface is  compatible  with  nneettaattaallkk  on
       BSD‐derived  systems.  Many BSD systems fail to check SSOO__BBRROOAADDCCAASSTT when
       sending broadcast frames; this can lead to compatibility problems.

       The raw socket mode is unique to Linux and exists to support the alter‐
       native CAP package and AppleTalk monitoring tools more easily.

